### Subsets (include/exclude pattern)
```java
public List<List<Integer>> subsets(int[] nums) {
    List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
    backtrack(nums, 0, new ArrayList<>(), res);
    return res;
}
void backtrack(int[] nums, int start, List<Integer> cur, List<List<Integer>> res) {
    res.add(new ArrayList<>(cur));
    for (int i = start; i < nums.length; i++) {
        cur.add(nums[i]);
        backtrack(nums, i + 1, cur, res);
        cur.remove(cur.size() - 1);
    }
}
```

### Combination Sum (reuse elements)
```java
void backtrack(int[] cands, int target, int start, List<Integer> cur, List<List<Integer>> res) {
    if (target == 0) { res.add(new ArrayList<>(cur)); return; }
    for (int i = start; i < cands.length && cands[i] <= target; i++) {
        cur.add(cands[i]);
        backtrack(cands, target - cands[i], i, cur, res); // i not i+1: reuse allowed
        cur.remove(cur.size() - 1);
    }
}
```

### Permutations
```java
void backtrack(int[] nums, boolean[] used, List<Integer> cur, List<List<Integer>> res) {
    if (cur.size() == nums.length) { res.add(new ArrayList<>(cur)); return; }
    for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
        if (used[i]) continue;
        used[i] = true; cur.add(nums[i]);
        backtrack(nums, used, cur, res);
        used[i] = false; cur.remove(cur.size() - 1);
    }
}
```

## Sorting Algorithms

### Merge Sort (stable, guaranteed O(n log n))
```java
void mergeSort(int[] arr, int l, int r) {
    if (l >= r) return;
    int mid = l + (r - l) / 2;
    mergeSort(arr, l, mid);
    mergeSort(arr, mid + 1, r);
    merge(arr, l, mid, r);
}
void merge(int[] arr, int l, int mid, int r) {
    int[] left = Arrays.copyOfRange(arr, l, mid + 1);
    int[] right = Arrays.copyOfRange(arr, mid + 1, r + 1);
    int i = 0, j = 0, k = l;
    while (i < left.length && j < right.length)
        arr[k++] = left[i] <= right[j] ? left[i++] : right[j++];
    while (i < left.length) arr[k++] = left[i++];
    while (j < right.length) arr[k++] = right[j++];
}
```

### Quick Sort (in-place, avg O(n log n), worst O(n²))
```java
void quickSort(int[] arr, int lo, int hi) {
    if (lo >= hi) return;
    int pivot = partition(arr, lo, hi);
    quickSort(arr, lo, pivot - 1);
    quickSort(arr, pivot + 1, hi);
}
int partition(int[] arr, int lo, int hi) {
    int pivot = arr[hi], i = lo;
    for (int j = lo; j < hi; j++)
        if (arr[j] <= pivot) { int t = arr[i]; arr[i++] = arr[j]; arr[j] = t; }
    int t = arr[i]; arr[i] = arr[hi]; arr[hi] = t;
    return i;
}
```

### Comparison
| Algorithm | Best | Average | Worst | Space | Stable |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Merge Sort | O(n log n) | O(n log n) | O(n log n) | O(n) | Yes |
| Quick Sort | O(n log n) | O(n log n) | O(n²) | O(log n) | No |
| Java Arrays.sort | - | O(n log n) | - | O(log n) | No* |
| Java Collections.sort | - | O(n log n) | - | O(n) | Yes |

## Trie Implementation

```java
class TrieNode {
    TrieNode[] children = new TrieNode[26];
    boolean isEnd = false;
    String word = null; // for Word Search II
}

class Trie {
    TrieNode root = new TrieNode();

    public void insert(String word) {
        TrieNode cur = root;
        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {
            int idx = c - 'a';
            if (cur.children[idx] == null) cur.children[idx] = new TrieNode();
            cur = cur.children[idx];
        }
        cur.isEnd = true;
    }

    public boolean search(String word) {
        TrieNode node = getNode(word);
        return node != null && node.isEnd;
    }

    public boolean startsWith(String prefix) {
        return getNode(prefix) != null;
    }

    private TrieNode getNode(String s) {
        TrieNode cur = root;
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            cur = cur.children[c - 'a'];
            if (cur == null) return null;
        }
        return cur;
    }
}
```

**Complexity:** Insert/Search/StartsWith all O(L) where L = word length. Space O(N×L×26).

### Word Search II (Trie + DFS on board)
Build Trie from all words, then DFS on each cell. Prune when no Trie node exists. Store word at leaf to avoid re-construction.

